  "commentary": {
    "theme": "A shot is a forcing combination that begins by giving something away. The first move offers a piece, or allows an exchange, and because captures are compulsory the opponent has no choice but to take it. That forced capture drags a piece onto a square where it can be jumped, opens a diagonal, or leaves a second piece without support, and the next move collects more than was invested. Shots are the heart of checkers tactics. To find one, do not start by asking which of your moves is safe. Ask instead where the opponent's pieces would have to go if you gave them a capture, and whether that new arrangement can be punished.",
